    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31700" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ob-littĕrātĭo</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oblīt-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, f.
		oblittero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a blotting out, erasing, effacing,
			obliteration;</i> and, in partic., <i>a blotting out
				from the memory, a forgetting, forgetfulness</i> (postAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aeris oblitteratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					34, 7, 18, § 47</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vetustatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 6, 194</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praeteritorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 30, 6, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
